  "observations": [
    "Optional subdomain restricts curve_length_parameters to a nonempty source interval. Returned parameters retain the original chart; before/after definitions still describe the complete source. Both oracle backends reject empty, reversed and out-of-domain intervals.",
    "The 96 native interval records contain 1,056 positions with repeated/reordered fractions, four inherited knot spacings, reverse traversal and shifted domains. Full value records, including lengths and unchanged sources, are compared at 1e-9.",
    "A failed native interval comparison exposed missing interior checkpoints on constant-speed NURBS spans. Scalar preparation now uses the shared Cash-Karp step schedule at unit speed, with affine distance accumulation and exact span lengths. Affine inversion between checkpoints retains the full batch capacity.",
    "Explicit geometric, quadrature-length and scalar-inverse trace modes retain existing diagnostic and length-only work limits. Analytic/polyline exact clocks and unequal-weight rational-line treatment are unchanged.",
    "Twenty-four frozen paired Loft cases vary only source knot spacing. Equal source images produce different fitted control counts. The separately measured interval stations agree physically across the four clocks to 2.6e-14, so these interval scalar samples do not explain the subdivision differences.",
    "No sampling heuristic or new adaptive command fit was admitted. The separate strict general scalar diagnostic still has 14 known curved-source mismatches among 2,090 queries; it remains unqualified."
  ],
